\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x,\n$$\n\nsolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+81y=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-9.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=-9,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=9A\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x-9B\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9=9A\\,⟹\\,A=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡9x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡9x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130353/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ebb2332-3e40-5627-bc43-258ca4a80424"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130374/selection/d6769641f3ce66654f4eaab17039fd30e6e32f15d6c33fe56e0d7f2453d311e4" :answer/id #uuid "12386fd2-1e92-5737-974b-8e0ecb06e956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130374/selection/f52418604ecc88de4fcefa8f7cd748951ef89526251bb7213f2dd457bb0d81b7" :answer/id #uuid "fb99c50e-69ed-5e37-832d-f5c79f6a79d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130374/selection/3c52373f30b8f5395705856635fba577755823d23cefc70b456d0b7eaffe34aa" :answer/id #uuid "489f0643-3c87-583d-94d8-598ec9538128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130374/selection/cdfa2b777d4e33941277f36f8b5751ae78463853b07ce85143a02eafef