$$\n\nThen, we substitute ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the above to get\n\n$$\n-P+Q=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $P=2$ gives $Q=0.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130374/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20e5f532-d99f-5406-b006-f34aa9074819"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130374"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
